  "verbalization": "The visible evidence from the hetionet dataset strongly suggests a mechanistic link between Iloperidone and Htr2a, mediated through Htr1d. Iloperidone binds to Htr1d, which is involved in multiple receptor activities, including serotonin receptor activity and G-protein coupled serotonin receptor activity. These activities are ultimately linked to Htr2a, indicating a pathway through which Iloperidone may influence Htr2a's function. The consistent scores across the three paths (0.6466, 0.6466, 0.505) suggest a robust and reliable interaction, though the third path has slightly lower confidence. The shared involvement of Htr1d in different receptor activities implies that Iloperidone may modulate Htr2a through a common intermediary, potentially affecting its role in signaling pathways. The evidence supports a mechanistic relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
